 "thesis": {
  "available": true,
  "why_on_the_list": "Compounder bucket, rank 32. Forward P/E 23.1, right at its four year median. Not cheap versus its own history, but revenue grew 24% last quarter with Cloud up 82% and a $514 billion Cloud backlog. It is on the list for quality and growth, with the entry point being the question.",
  "business_quality": "Search is still a 90% share product and grew 17% last quarter to $63.3 billion despite AI Overviews and chat competitors. Cloud has become a second engine: $24.8 billion of quarterly revenue with operating income of $8.8 billion versus $2.8 billion a year earlier. The December 2025 antitrust judgment left Chrome and Android intact but imposed data sharing and default restrictions. Insider ownership is about 1.6%.",
  "verdict": "Buy on pullback, November tranche or earlier if the zone is hit. Buy zone $300 to $335. Conviction 3 of 5.",
  "action": "Buy on pullback, November tranche or earlier if the zone is hit",
  "conviction": 3,
